**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The kit window attaches a file through the wizard, by semantic messages (001 §P `AttachDataFile`; 001 §K: a named profile is saved in `.kit-json`; the S9.2 brief: AttachDataFile takes the file, copies it in or records it in place (S4.2), applies a profile and gives mapped points; .spec-md §4 'UI': the button and the test send the same message, and the window hosts a new surface through messages). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2: (1) `KitWindowShell` (steps 186, 201, 225) gains `openImportWizard : ImportWizardRequest -> unit` (opens the wizard over a request, step 311), documented in one line; `inert` holds `ignore`, and every shell built as an update of `inert` (step 201) is unchanged. (2) `AttachDataFileTo` (steps 135, 291, 295) is renamed `AttachDataFile of Experiments.ExperimentId * FileName * ImportProfileName` (attach the picked file and map it by that profile), its doc saying so: its arm records `profile` from the message where it recorded the detector's `builtInProfile`, with `rows = AllDataRows`, and everything else in it — the read-only guard (step 185), the attach, the record, the badge and the refusal's `kitStatus` (step 295) — is unchanged. (3) New messages, each documented in one line and behind the read-only guard of step 185 (`The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.`, nothing opened or written): `OpenImportWizard of Experiments.ExperimentId * FileName`, the Attach data file… button's message after its file dialog: for an experiment the collection holds, it calls `model.kitShell.openImportWizard { experimentId; file; readPickedFile = model.experimentData.readPickedFile; kitProfiles = model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles; defaultProfile = (detectorKindOf model.library <the experiment's slots>).builtInProfile }` (steps 291, 305) and answers the model unchanged; an experiment it lacks changes nothing. `SaveImportProfile of ImportProfile`, the wizard's new mapping: `model.kit.kitFile.withImportProfile` (step 299), whose `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved — <e.describe>` and writes nothing, and whose `Ok kitFile` is written by `model.kit.saveKitFile kitFile` (step 131): `Ok kit` makes `model.kit` that context and `kitStatus` `Saved the import profile '<name>'.`, and `Error e` keeps the model and sets `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`, as `SaveNamingTemplate` does (step 273). The window's own write is not a change offered for reload (step 130). (4) `type ImportWizardApplied with member this.messages : TableAndElementRotationMsg list`, the wizard's Attach as the window's messages: `SaveImportProfile p` when `savedOpt` is `Some p`, then `AttachDataFile (experimentId, file, profile)`, so a new profile is in the kit before a file is mapped by it. (5) `attachDataFileButton` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:attachDataFileButton`, steps 135, 241) sends `OpenImportWizard (experiment.id, file)` on a confirmed pick where it sent `AttachDataFileTo`; the picker and its folder memory are unchanged. No other message, field or option is added. Tests. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184), over a folder kit holding an experiment `E1` (a one-axis R1 scan over 0…360°, as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:filledExperiments` builds one) loaded into `initInverse` with a recording shell: `Save import profile writes the wizard's new mapping into the kit file and refuses a name the kit holds`: `SaveImportProfile` of a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column) leaves `model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles` and `readKitFile ()` holding it and `kitStatus` `Saved the import profile 'Lab scan'.`, and a second send sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not saved —` and holding `already holds`, the `.kit-json` bytes unchanged. `opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default`: after `SaveImportProfile` of `Lab scan`, `OpenImportWizard (ExperimentId 1, <a test-local file>)` records one request with that id and file, `kitProfiles` holding `Lab scan` and `defaultProfile` `Intensity series`, and leaves the model unchanged. `the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it`: `messages` of an applied `{ ExperimentId 1; <a Phone ROI file written outside the kit as the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,1,2026-07-15T12:05:00+00:00,45,912.25\n`>; Phone ROI by columns; Some <a test-local profile `Phone ROI by columns`: comma, a header row, the mark, scan column 4 in degrees as a physical value, `SignalColumns (5, None)`, timestamp 3, capture index 2, key 1> }` are `[ SaveImportProfile <it>; AttachDataFile (ExperimentId 1, <the file>, Phone ROI by columns) ]`; passed through the update in order, they leave the kit file holding the profile, E1's `dataOpt` holding an attachment at `data/<the file's leaf>` mapped by `Phone ROI by columns` over every row, its file read back through `readExperiments` holding the same, and `model.dataBadgeOf E1` `ValidatedDataBadge` of 2 points. `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` (step 185) also sends `OpenImportWizard`, `SaveImportProfile` and `AttachDataFile`, with its assertions and an empty shell recorder. `InverseConstructorTests`: every `AttachDataFileTo` it dispatches becomes `AttachDataFile` with `ImportProfileName.intensitySeries`, or `ellipsometricSeries` for the ellipsometric fixture, every assertion kept (`attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status` and `a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why`); `the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path` is renamed `the profile the wizard chose selects the ellipsometric read`, dispatching `ellipsometricSeries`, its assertions kept. `DataFilePickerFolderTests` passes as written. After this step `git grep -n -F "AttachDataFileTo" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the kit window attaches through the wizard, `OpenImportWizard` MUST hand the shell a request with the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default, `SaveImportProfile` MUST write a new profile into the kit file and refuse a held or built-in name, `AttachDataFile` MUST attach the file by the profile it names, `ImportWizardApplied.messages` MUST save before it attaches, a read-only kit MUST refuse all three, and `git grep -n -F "AttachDataFileTo" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Save import profile writes the wizard's new mapping into the kit file and refuses a name the kit holds`, `opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default` and `the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including the renamed `the profile the wizard chose selects the ellipsometric read` and the changed `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status` and `a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why`, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
